{"id":"n1dff8e833603","url":"https://www.dental-tribune.com/news/hassbio-launches-amber-drymill/","title":"HASSBIO expands Amber DryMill range ahead of IDS 2027","source":"Dental Tribune","date":"2026-11-25T15:02:52.000Z","byline":"HASSBIO","image":"https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/39be7c2e/cmVzaXplLWNyb3Aodz0xNjA7aD0xNjApOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD1naWYp/wp-content/themes/dt/images/company-photo.gif","imageKind":"","imageBg":"","html":"<img src=\"https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/39be7c2e/cmVzaXplLWNyb3Aodz0xNjA7aD0xNjApOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD1naWYp/wp-content/themes/dt/images/company-photo.gif\" alt=\"HASSBIO\" loading=\"lazy\"> <p>HASSBIO</p> <p>Wed. 25. November 2026</p> share save <h2><p>GANGNEUNG, South Korea: HASSBIO, a global pioneer in dental prosthetic materials, has expanded its Amber DryMill product range with the commercial launch of a disc version in South Korea and Thailand this month. Developed for dry-milling workflows, the lithium disilicate material was presented at the Korea Dental Technology Expo &amp; Scientific Conference in July. The company is now preparing for its international launch.</p>\n</h2> <p>At the HASSBIO booth, dental technicians were able to learn about Amber DryMill and its use in dry-milling workflows. Additionally, the company presented information on the material’s microstructure and how it is intended to support dry-milling performance. HASSBIO also outlined the Amber DryMill evaluation programme, through which participants test the material and provide feedback.</p>\n<h2>Edge stability during dry milling</h2>\n<p>Amber DryMill combines suitability for dry milling with the optical and bonding properties associated with lithium disilicate. According to the company, the material’s microstructure has been designed to facilitate dry milling and maintain edge stability, even at thin restoration margins. HASSBIO also noted that the material may help reduce milling bur wear, potentially improving productivity and extending bur service life.</p>\n<h2>Optical properties and adhesive cementation</h2>\n<p>According to HASSBIO, the material exhibits fluorescence and light transmission properties that support a natural-looking appearance. The company says that restorations fabricated from the material can be etched with hydrofluoric acid and adhesively cemented according to established protocols for lithium disilicate.</p>\n<h2>International launch planned for 2027</h2>\n<p>According to HASSBIO, Amber DryMill received regulatory approval in South Korea and Thailand earlier this year. The material is intended for use with compatible laboratory milling systems and was initially available in block form. The company confirmed that the disc version became commercially available in South Korea and Thailand this month, expanding the product range for dental laboratories.</p>\n<p>HASSBIO is planning to expand distribution as Amber DryMill receives regulatory approval in additional markets. According to the company, regulatory approval remains pending in Brazil, Europe, Japan and the US. HASSBIO intends to introduce the material to international markets at the 2027 International Dental Show, which will take place from 16 to 20 March in Cologne in Germany.</p>\n<p>At the event, HASSBIO plans to present its complete Amber DryMill product range. Visitors will have the opportunity to experience the material first hand and learn more about its applications in dry-milling workflows. Further information on the material, including its processing protocols and product range, is available on <a href=\"https://www.hassbio.com/en/products/106\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">the HASSBIO website</a>.</p>\n<picture><source srcset=\"https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/035adaa9/cmVzaXplKHc9MTMyMDtoPTc0Myk6c2hhcnBlbihsZXZlbD0wKTpvdXRwdXQoZm9ybWF0PXdlYnAp/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 1320w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/a92a1c9a/cmVzaXplKHc9Mjk3O2g9MTY4KTpzaGFycGVuKGxldmVsPTApOm91dHB1dChmb3JtYXQ9d2VicCk/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 297w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/d29c4696/cmVzaXplKHc9NDYyO2g9MjYxKTpzaGFycGVuKGxldmVsPTApOm91dHB1dChmb3JtYXQ9d2VicCk/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 462w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/61210002/cmVzaXplKHc9NjYwO2g9MzcyKTpzaGFycGVuKGxldmVsPTApOm91dHB1dChmb3JtYXQ9d2VicCk/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 660w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/54515a17/cmVzaXplKHc9OTkwO2g9NTU4KTpzaGFycGVuKGxldmVsPTApOm91dHB1dChmb3JtYXQ9d2VicCk/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 990w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/247b7b24/cmVzaXplKHc9MTY1MDtoPTkyOSk6c2hhcnBlbihsZXZlbD0wKTpvdXRwdXQoZm9ybWF0PXdlYnAp/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 1650w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/4852e7c6/cmVzaXplKHc9MTk4MDtoPTExMTUpOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD13ZWJwKQ/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 1980w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/47153d1d/cmVzaXplKHc9MjMxMDtoPTEzMDEpOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD13ZWJwKQ/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 2310w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/56794e34/cmVzaXplKHc9MjY0MDtoPTE0ODYpOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD13ZWJwKQ/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 2640w\" type=\"image/webp\"> <source srcset=\"https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/81817ec1/cmVzaXplKHc9MTMyMDtoPTc0Myk6c2hhcnBlbihsZXZlbD0wKTpvdXRwdXQoZm9ybWF0PXBuZyk/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 1320w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/d6605d2b/cmVzaXplKHc9Mjk3O2g9MTY4KTpzaGFycGVuKGxldmVsPTApOm91dHB1dChmb3JtYXQ9cG5nKQ/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 297w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/df9f8240/cmVzaXplKHc9NDYyO2g9MjYxKTpzaGFycGVuKGxldmVsPTApOm91dHB1dChmb3JtYXQ9cG5nKQ/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 462w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/926f4de3/cmVzaXplKHc9NjYwO2g9MzcyKTpzaGFycGVuKGxldmVsPTApOm91dHB1dChmb3JtYXQ9cG5nKQ/up/dt/2026/07/Amber-DryMill_2.png 660w, https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti